---
import Document from '../layouts/Document.astro';
import { supportEmail } from '../site.mjs';
---

<Document title="Terms of Service" description="Read the terms for using ColdCorners and coldcorners.app, including the Mac App Store license, purchases, and how to contact the developer." updated="2026-11-21">
  <section>
    <h2>Mac App Store license and purchases</h2>
    <p>Copies of ColdCorners obtained through the Mac App Store are governed by the license offered with the app. <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Apple's Standard End User License Agreement</a> applies unless a custom license is provided with the app.</p>
    <p>The store shows the applicable price, availability, and purchase conditions. Apple handles App Store payments and refunds. <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Apple purchase support</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Using ColdCorners</h2>
    <p>You choose Hot Corner actions in macOS and the displays and corners where they can activate in ColdCorners. Blocking requires the app to be running with the requested system permission. Check your selections when you change your display setup. You can disable the app, quit it, or revoke the permission at any time.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Website and external services</h2>
    <p>Use this website and its support channels lawfully and respect other people's rights. The developer provides product information and help and may update them as ColdCorners changes. Original content and branding belong to their respective owners. Third-party materials retain their applicable licenses.</p>
    <p>External services, including Apple and GitHub, have their own terms. The <a href="/privacy-policy/">ColdCorners Privacy Policy</a> explains how the app, the website, and support handle information.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Availability and your rights</h2>
    <p>The website is provided as available. Compatibility can vary with macOS updates and display configurations. The app's applicable license sets out its warranty and liability terms. These terms preserve rights and remedies that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>Updates to these terms will appear on this page with a new date. For questions about the terms, email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. For help using the app, visit <a href="/support/">ColdCorners Support</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Document>
